From: DroidDeck
Subject: [PATCH] rendervulkan: linear when the backend offers no modifier

A game on Mali asked for a 10-bit (A2B10G10R10) swapchain, the nested backend offered no
modifier for that format, and gamescope aborted on assert( !modifiers.empty() ), taking the
session down. It now falls back to the linear modifier.
---
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -2243,9 +2243,19 @@
 		else
 		{
 			std::span<const uint64_t> modifiers = GetBackend()->GetSupportedModifiers( drmFormat );
-			assert( !modifiers.empty() );
-			possibleModifiers = modifiers.data();
-			numPossibleModifiers = modifiers.size();
+			if ( modifiers.empty() )
+			{
+				// The host compositor offers no modifier for this format (the app's Android
+				// compositor takes 8-bit RGB only, and a game asked for a 10-bit swapchain):
+				// fall back to linear rather than abort the whole session.
+				possibleModifiers = &linear;
+				numPossibleModifiers = 1;
+			}
+			else
+			{
+				possibleModifiers = modifiers.data();
+				numPossibleModifiers = modifiers.size();
+			}
 		}
 
 		for ( size_t i = 0; i < numPossibleModifiers; i++ )
